-- title:
--   Decomposition-stable admissible small constants for q=2
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q=2$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number not divisible by $q$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` satisfying `LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. the image of $q$ lies in $A$ and is a nonunit there. Then there exist an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\mathbb Q \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ and an element $\pi_0 \in k_0$ whose image lies in $A$ such that, writing $A_0$ for the pullback of $A$ along $k_0 \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb Q}$ (so $A_0 = A \cap k_0$), the following hold: $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring whose maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$; $A_0$ is a henselian local ring; the residue field of $A_0$ is algebraically closed; every $a \in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to some $c \in k_0$ with $c \in A$; and $k_0$ is stable under every $\mathbb Q$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $x \in A \iff \tau x \in A$ for all $x$. Moreover there is a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \ge 3$, $\ell \ne q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$, an element $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ which is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and an element $\varpi_t \in k_0$ lying in $A$ together with a unit $u$ of $A$ such that $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$.
--
--   This provides the ring of "small constants" used when working $q$-adically over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$: a henselian discrete valuation subring of a subfield $k_0$, with algebraically closed residue field surjecting onto that of $A$, stable under the decomposition group of $A$, and equipped with an auxiliary prime $\ell$ prime to $qM'$, a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity and a root of $q$ of degree $q^2-1$ up to units. It is the $q=2$ case, and is used in the construction of Igusa-type smooth charts on modular curves of full level and in the downstream statement on admissible small constants for $q=2$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ValuationSubring_exists_admissible_smallConstants_stable_of_eq_two.lean

